## What the official site says

[Rockstar’s GTA VI page](https://www.rockstargames.com/VI), checked on 8 November 2026, still says the game is coming November 19, 2026 for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S. The same page says pre-load begins November 10, and it labels PlayStation 5 as the platform it plays best on. That page does not list a PC date.

Treat November 19 as Rockstar’s stated target, not a promise that the date cannot move. If it changes, the change belongs on Rockstar’s page.

This is a separate game from Grand Theft Auto V Enhanced, which is already released on PC. The Enhanced edition has its own [Steam listing](/apps/gta-v-enhanced).

## Official updates already posted

On October 15, 2026, Rockstar featured the GTA VI launch trailer on its newswire. Watch that video on [Rockstar’s trailer post](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/517572321a549a), not a re-upload. That post was still available on 8 November 2026.

On October 8, 2026, Rockstar posted about the in-game radio stations and the music of Leonida. The lineup and details are in [that announcement](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/o3982oa93a23k4/the-music-of-grand-theft-auto-vi-in-game-radio-stations). That post was still available on 8 November 2026.

## What this page does not claim

This is a dated editorial snapshot. It is not a hands-on preview, a PC release date, or a list of system requirements. GameNews is not affiliated with Rockstar. When a newer official post appears, use the publisher’s page rather than an older recap.
